### Product API requests
### Update baseUrl to match your running product service or gateway.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8083
@productId = 1
@searchKeyword = phone

### 1) Create product
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Demo Phone",
  "description": "6.5 inch OLED screen",
  "price": 699.99,
  "stockQuantity": 25,
  "category": "Electronics",
  "imageUrl": "https://example.com/images/demo-phone.jpg"
}

> {%
  // Save the created product id for follow-up requests.
  client.global.set("productId", response.body.id);
%}

### 2) Get all products
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

### 3) Get product by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}

### 4) Update product
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Demo Phone Pro",
  "description": "Updated model with more storage",
  "price": 799.99,
  "stockQuantity": 18,
  "category": "Electronics",
  "imageUrl": "https://example.com/images/demo-phone-pro.jpg"
}

### 5) Search products by keyword
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/search?keyword={{searchKeyword}}

### 6) Delete product
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}

### 7) Verify product deletion (expects 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{productId}}

